# 23. Important improvement: reservation vs consumption

Recommended lifecycle:

```text
ORDER CREATED
      ↓
LETTER RESERVED
      ↓
LETTER PRINTED
      ↓
LETTER PACKED
      ↓
LETTER SHIPPED
      ↓
LETTER DELIVERED
```

The system must explicitly define when a letter becomes "consumed".

Recommended default:

```text
CONSUMED = PRINTED
```

if printing means it physically enters the package and cannot be reused.

Alternative:

```text
CONSUMED = PACKED
```

if reprinting before packing should reuse the same letter.

Make this a configuration/business rule.

---

# 24. Reprint behavior

A reprint of the same order must NOT allocate the next story letter.

Example:

```text
Order #1001
Letter #43
Template #4
```

If manufacturer clicks print again:

```text
Still Letter #43
Same allocation
Same rendered snapshot
```

unless an admin explicitly voids/replaces it.

This is critical.

---

# 25. Idempotency

The print endpoint must accept an idempotency key.

Example:

```http
POST /orders/{orderId}/personalized-letter/print
Idempotency-Key: 8f0c...
```

Store the key and resulting allocation.

Repeated request:

```text
same idempotency key
        ↓
return existing result
```

Also enforce database uniqueness by order.

Do not rely on idempotency keys alone.

