# 45. Story editing rules

If a story letter has never been consumed:

```text
Editable
```

If a letter has already been delivered:

```text
Do not mutate historical version.
Create a new version.
```

Recommended:

```text
story_letter_versions
```

if the business expects frequent edits.

Alternative simpler initial approach:

- Draft edits allowed before publication.
- Published letters are immutable.
- Corrections create a new version.

---

# 46. Story versioning

If stories can be changed substantially after customers have started them, add:

```sql
story_versions
```

with:

```text
id
story_id
version_number
status
created_at
published_at
```

and connect letters to a story version.

If the product requirement is that stories are immutable after publication, this can be deferred.

Recommended initial rule:

> Published story letter content is immutable; corrections create versions.

This keeps the first implementation simpler while preserving historical correctness.

---

# 47. Handling deleted/paused stories

Never delete a story that has historical deliveries.

If a story is paused:

```text
New customer -> not assigned
Existing customer -> continue or stop according to configuration
```

If archived:

```text
Never newly assigned
```

If an active customer is currently assigned to an archived story:

- preserve historical assignment
- define whether next letter can continue
- if continuation is prohibited, transition the customer to another story through a controlled transaction

Never silently lose customer progress.

---

# 48. Story completion edge case

If:

```text
next_sequence_number = 101
```

but Story has only 100 active letters:

This is not a normal request error.

It indicates a story completion condition.

Transactionally:

```text
complete Story A
assign Story B
allocate Story B / Letter 1
```

If no eligible next story exists:

```text
complete Story A
no next story
customer_story status = COMPLETED
customer has no active story
```

The order should receive a clearly defined result:

```text
LETTER_NOT_AVAILABLE
```

or the system should have a fallback/default story policy.

Do not fabricate a letter.

---

# 49. No eligible story policy

Admin must be able to configure what happens when no next story is available.

Options:

```text
WAIT
USE_FALLBACK_STORY
DISABLE_PERSONALIZED_LETTER
```

Default recommendation:

```text
DISABLE_PERSONALIZED_LETTER
```

with an observable warning rather than assigning an invalid story.

