# 55. Security

Template rendering must be sandboxed.

Prevent:

- arbitrary code execution
- SQL injection through templates
- server-side template injection
- unsafe HTML
- malicious file paths
- unrestricted network access

Sanitize output if HTML is displayed in browser.

If PDFs are generated, only render trusted/sanitized content.

Admin-only operations require authorization checks on the backend, not only UI hiding.

Manufacturer endpoints must verify manufacturer ownership/access to the order.

